[Page:Glossary]
SectionPrefix=Term

[Term:ball:Ball A and ball B]
Ball A is the ball the game serves. Ball B joins it when the game puts a second
one into play.

[Term:ball_state_record:Ball state record]
Everything the game knows about one ball in flight – where it is heading, how
fast, and what it last bounced off. Ball A and ball B each have one.

[Term:brick_index:Brick index]
A brick's place in the brick field as a single number, 0 to 80. It counts along
each row in turn.

[Term:brick_slot:Brick slot]
One of the 81 positions in the brick field. A slot may contain a brick or be empty.

[Term:brick_state_map:Brick state map]
One entry per brick slot: the class of its break animation and the current
sub-frame of that animation, or none for a settled slot. An entry that holds
the finished marker has a revealed glyph at rest in the cell.


[Term:dirty_counter:Dirty counter]
A mark on one screen cell. It says the cell's picture changed and the screen does not
show it yet.

[Term:durability_class:Durability class]
How a brick stands up to hits: how many hits it survives, and what it
leaves behind when it breaks.

[Term:frame:Frame]
One pass of the game's main loop. It lasts as long as that pass's work takes.


[Term:heading_code:Heading code]
Which way a ball or another object travels, as one of 72 headings around the
circle.

[Term:level_index:Level index]
Which level record is in play, counted from 0.

[Term:logic_record:Logic record]
An object's movement state: its heading, its speed and its animation frame.


[Term:losing_edge:Losing edge]
The edge the bat plays from, where a ball that gets past it is lost.

[Term:object_pool:Object pool]
The nine slots that hold everything the game moves and draws.

[Term:pool_slot:Pool slot]
One of the object pool's nine places.


[Term:principal_heading:Principal heading]
One of eight headings: the four along the axes, and the four diagonals at 41°,
139°, 221° and 319°.

[Term:return_window:Return window]
The band around the bat inside which a ball counts as returned.

[Term:slot_code:Slot code]
What the level designer put in a brick slot: which brick design stands there, or
nothing.

[Term:source_bank:Source bank]
The sprite bitmaps as loaded, from which the sprite bank is filled.

[Term:sprite_bank:Sprite bank]
The sprite bitmaps the game draws from, one 16×16 bitmap per animation frame.

[Term:terminator:Terminator]
A byte that marks the end of a run whose length is not written down.

[Term:tile_code:Tile code]
Which 8×8 picture stands in a cell of the tile map.

[Term:tilemap:Tile map]
What stands in every cell of the screen, one tile code per cell. This is the
surface the game reads to find out what is in a cell.

[Term:wave_script:Wave script]
The eight things a level can spawn. Each one is an object type, or nothing.

[Term:work_buffer:Work buffer]
The dirty counters, one per screen cell.

